{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QcmvrY1tWjzo48AuP9yjhR","type":"tool_result","content":"170\tThe graph must support exact identity lookup, bounded neighborhood traversal, impact queries, doc/code backlinks, and freshness queries.\n171\t\n172\t### 3. Event Log\n173\t\n174\tThe event log is append-only and replayable. It is the substrate that makes memory consolidation and usefulness measurement possible.\n175\t\n176\tRequired event types:\n177\t\n178\t- `AssistantTaskStarted`\n179\t- `ToolCalled`\n180\t- `ToolResult`\n181\t- `ContextBundleReturned`\n182\t- `MemoryRetrieved`\n183\t- `MemoryExpanded`\n184\t- `PlanCreated`\n185\t- `FileRead`\n186\t- `PatchApplied`\n187\t- `TestRunStarted`\n188\t- `TestRunCompleted`\n189\t- `DiagnosticObserved`\n190\t- `UserCorrection`\n191\t- `UserPreferenceObserved`\n192\t- `WorkflowSucceeded`\n193\t- `WorkflowFailed`\n194\t- `MemoryCreated`\n195\t- `MemoryUpdated`\n196\t- `MemoryInvalidated`\n197\t- `MemoryConsolidated`\n198\t\n199\tEvents should carry:\n200\t\n201\t- workspace id\n202\t- branch\n203\t- session id\n204\t- task id\n205\t- actor\n206\t- timestamp\n207\t- stable references to files, symbols, docs, events, and memories\n208\t- payload hash\n209\t- compact payload summary\n210\t- optional full payload location\n211\t\n212\tThe full event stream should not be injected into prompts. It exists for retrieval, audit, replay, metrics, and consolidation.\n213\t\n214\t### 4. Memory Graph\n215\t\n216\tMemory should be stored as typed claims and episodes, not loose notes.\n217\t\n218\tPrimary memory classes:\n219\t\n220\t- `Observation`\n221\t- `Decision`\n222\t- `Constraint`\n223\t- `Pattern`\n224\t- `AntiPattern`\n225\t- `WorkflowOutcome`\n226\t- `FailurePattern`\n227\t- `Procedure`\n228\t- `Preference`\n229\t- `ArchitectureInvariant`\n230\t- `DocsContract`\n231\t- `OpenQuestion`\n232\t- `CounterMemory` — a memory record that explicitly asserts a prior memory is wrong or no longer applicable. Distinct from a `contradicts` link: a link connects two existing memories; a CounterMemory is a first-class record authored by an agent or user that carries its own evidence, scope, and verification status and can itself be superseded or invalidated. Use CounterMemory when the counter-claim needs its own provenance and lifecycle, not just an edge annotation.\n233\t\n234\tEach memory record requires:\n235\t\n236\t- stable id\n237\t- content\n238\t- memory class\n239\t- assertion type\n240\t- scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization\n241\t- verification status\n242\t- confidence and confidence reason\n243\t- freshness policy\n244\t- validity conditions\n245\t- invalidation triggers\n246\t- provenance events\n247\t- evidence references\n248\t- linked files\n249\t- linked symbols\n250\t- linked docs\n251\t- linked tests\n252\t- linked memories\n253\t- contradiction links\n254\t- supersession links\n255\t- access history\n256\t- usefulness scores\n257\t- last verified state\n258\t\n259\tMemory links should be first-class records:\n260\t\n261\t- source memory\n262\t- target memory or graph node\n263\t- link type\n264\t- strength\n265\t- reason\n266\t- evidence event\n267\t- created by\n268\t- created at\n269\t- verification status"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b8088fa-bb22-4ad9-a735-7b2a3a41ef4e","uuid":"f34978b9-691f-4110-866e-aa61d717127a","timestamp":"2026-05-17T05:57:29.976Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"The graph must support exact identity lookup, bounded neighborhood traversal, impact queries, doc/code backlinks, and freshness queries.\n\n### 3. Event Log\n\nThe event log is append-only and replayable. It is the substrate that makes memory consolidation and usefulness measurement possible.\n\nRequired event types:\n\n- `AssistantTaskStarted`\n- `ToolCalled`\n- `ToolResult`\n- `ContextBundleReturned`\n- `MemoryRetrieved`\n- `MemoryExpanded`\n- `PlanCreated`\n- `FileRead`\n- `PatchApplied`\n- `TestRunStarted`\n- `TestRunCompleted`\n- `DiagnosticObserved`\n- `UserCorrection`\n- `UserPreferenceObserved`\n- `WorkflowSucceeded`\n- `WorkflowFailed`\n- `MemoryCreated`\n- `MemoryUpdated`\n- `MemoryInvalidated`\n- `MemoryConsolidated`\n\nEvents should carry:\n\n- workspace id\n- branch\n- session id\n- task id\n- actor\n- timestamp\n- stable references to files, symbols, docs, events, and memories\n- payload hash\n- compact payload summary\n- optional full payload location\n\nThe full event stream should not be injected into prompts. It exists for retrieval, audit, replay, metrics, and consolidation.\n\n### 4. Memory Graph\n\nMemory should be stored as typed claims and episodes, not loose notes.\n\nPrimary memory classes:\n\n- `Observation`\n- `Decision`\n- `Constraint`\n- `Pattern`\n- `AntiPattern`\n- `WorkflowOutcome`\n- `FailurePattern`\n- `Procedure`\n- `Preference`\n- `ArchitectureInvariant`\n- `DocsContract`\n- `OpenQuestion`\n- `CounterMemory` — a memory record that explicitly asserts a prior memory is wrong or no longer applicable. Distinct from a `contradicts` link: a link connects two existing memories; a CounterMemory is a first-class record authored by an agent or user that carries its own evidence, scope, and verification status and can itself be superseded or invalidated. Use CounterMemory when the counter-claim needs its own provenance and lifecycle, not just an edge annotation.\n\nEach memory record requires:\n\n- stable id\n- content\n- memory class\n- assertion type\n- scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization\n- verification status\n- confidence and confidence reason\n- freshness policy\n- validity conditions\n- invalidation triggers\n- provenance events\n- evidence references\n- linked files\n- linked symbols\n- linked docs\n- linked tests\n- linked memories\n- contradiction links\n- supersession links\n- access history\n- usefulness scores\n- last verified state\n\nMemory links should be first-class records:\n\n- source memory\n- target memory or graph node\n- link type\n- strength\n- reason\n- evidence event\n- created by\n- created at\n- verification status","numLines":100,"startLine":170,"totalLines":969}}}
